# Explain the work after each task

When you finish a task the user asked you to do (implement, fix, or change docs), do not only list commands. Explain the work so they can talk about it.

## Order

1. What changed, in everyday words. What a person can now do that they could not do before.
2. How it was built. Name the files and functions. Define a term the first time you use it.
3. Why you chose that shape, in one or two reasons. If you rejected an obvious alternative, say so in one line.
4. Then the test commands they can run.

## Voice

- Simple first. Technical names second.
- Short paragraphs or a short bullet list. Not a dump of every file.
- Do not open with jargon, a file tree, or “we refactored the auth layer.”

## Do not

- Skip this after a slice, a bug fix, or a docs change they asked for.
- Recap when they only asked a question. Answer the question first, then only the facts they need to act.
